    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>The C&amp;D waste treatment in mobile recycling facilities consists of a sequence of physical and mechanical steps, including crushing, metal separation, sieving, and manual/mechanical sorting to remove the impurities such as wood, paper, and plastic. Mobile plants are fuelled by diesel and usually involve fewer treatment processes (manual sorting is usually adopted, and waste sieving may be optional). Generally, produce all-in aggregates (e.g. classes 0/63 mm, 0/80 mm, 0/90 mm). &#13;
&#13;
Good the Reliability;   &#13;
Very Good the Geographical representativeness;   &#13;
Very Good the Time representativeness;   &#13;
Very Good the Technological representativeness. </technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>On-site recycling of inert waste deriving from construction and demolition activities.</technologicalApplicability>
    </technology>
  </processInformation>
